# Competitive Research: {{PRODUCT_NAME}}

Competitive intelligence system tracking {{COMPETITOR_COUNT}} competitors in {{INDUSTRY}}.

## Key Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| reference/product-info.md | {{PRODUCT_NAME}} positioning & capabilities |
| reference/competitors.md | Master competitor list |
| reference/guidelines.md | Profile template ({{SECTION_COUNT}} sections) |

## Rules

1. All profiles must follow the template in reference/guidelines.md
2. Label all claims: `- Observed:` (with URL) or `- Inferred (assumption):`
3. Add new competitors to reference/competitors.md first
4. Preserve and refine existing content - don't delete without reason

## Commands

- `/setup` - Reconfigure (use --product, --competitors, or --template to update specific parts)
- `/competitive-update` - Research competitors for updates (--all, --competitor <name>, --update)
- `/generate-analysis <topic>` - Generate cross-competitor analysis on any dimension
- Or just ask naturally: "How does everyone handle pricing?" triggers analysis with confirmation

## Workflow

1. Start with `/competitive-update --all` to populate profiles
2. Review and refine profiles as you learn more
3. Ask questions or run `/generate-analysis` for cross-competitor insights
4. Re-run `/competitive-update` periodically to stay current
